WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.077 --> 00:00:02.720
INTRO:
Jack Ma is one of the few men in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:09.280
the entire world who have been able to create over&nbsp;
$1 trillion worth of value in the market. He’s the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:15.520
man behind some of the largest Chinese companies&nbsp;
including Alibaba, the Ant Group, and Cainiao.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:20.880
Hearing this, I don’t think you’d be surprised&nbsp;
to hear that Jack was the richest man in China&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:28.240
not too long ago with a peak net worth of $61.2&nbsp;
billion. Over the past two years, however, his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:36.400
net worth has tumbled nearly 50% to $32.3 billion.&nbsp;
At first glance, it’s easy to dismiss this as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:42.400
side effects of a weak stock market or an economic&nbsp;
downturn. But, if we take a closer look at Jack’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:49.440
story, we’ll see that this downfall was anything&nbsp;
but natural. You see, the reason Jack Ma has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:55.440
getting destroyed is actually because he said&nbsp;
some not so great things about the CCP or the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.440 --> 00:01:03.520
Chinese Communist Party. Obviously, the CCP wasn’t&nbsp;
very happy about his perspectives, so they decided&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:09.840
to teach him a lesson. And if you thought Jack’s&nbsp;
decline in net worth was already pretty bad, well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:16.320
that’s the least of it. The CCP has gone ahead and&nbsp;
demolished the valuations of all of his companies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:23.840
Take Alibaba for example. In October of 2020,&nbsp;
Alibaba reached a peak valuation of $858 billion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:32.160
By March of 2022, however, Alibaba would shed 77%&nbsp;
of this valuation crashing down to $206 billion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:40.000
That works out to a market cap loss of $652&nbsp;
billion and that’s just Alibaba. Moving onto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:45.680
the Ant Group, this company was just about to&nbsp;
IPO right before all of this drama unfolded.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:52.240
And according to Forbes, it was realistic to&nbsp;
estimate up to a $470 billion valuation. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:57.600
once Jack shared his comments, Beijing would halt&nbsp;
the IPO and essentially force Jack to hand over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:03.360
the entire company to the CCP. It appears that&nbsp;
Jack tried to stall this as much as possible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:09.360
but he eventually caved in all the way in late&nbsp;
July. Today, Fidelity values the Ant Group at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:14.960
just $70 billion which is $400 billion&nbsp;
less than their projected IPO valuation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:19.920
If we add this market cap loss to the Alibaba’s&nbsp;
market cap loss of $652 billion, we get a total&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:27.840
market cap loss of $1.05 trillion with a T.&nbsp;
And that’s just Jack’s largest companies. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:32.560
we threw all of his other smaller companies into&nbsp;
the mix, we’ll see that Jack has endured a market&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:40.000
cap loss of $1.1 to $1.2 trillion within the past&nbsp;
24 months. His losses alone are enough to create&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:49.840
the world’s 6th largest company. So, what in the&nbsp;
world did Jack do to deserve such a punishment?

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:51.520
THE FATEFUL SPEECH:&nbsp;

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:57.200
Taking a look back, all of Jack’s problems can be&nbsp;
traced back to one fateful speech on October 24,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:02.720
2020 at the Bund Summit. Jack was well aware&nbsp;
of the weight of what he was about to share,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:08.000
so he started off with a little disclaimer. He&nbsp;
asserted that his views are probably immature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:13.680
incorrect, and laughable. He also suggested that&nbsp;
people should simply give him a listen and if he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:19.120
doesn’t make any sense, they should forget about&nbsp;
everything he said. With that out of the way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:24.560
Jack began discussing the role of China in the&nbsp;
global economy. He argued that China had basically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:29.920
become someone that fills in the gaps left by the&nbsp;
west. For example, the west doesn’t want to take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:35.840
on low paying manufacturing jobs, so China fills&nbsp;
in the gap. Similarly, the west doesn’t want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:41.680
pollute their own ecosystems with factories, so&nbsp;
China fills in the gap. Jack argued that instead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:46.960
of filling in the gaps left behind by the west,&nbsp;
China should look to fill in gaps in the future.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:52.160
This way, China could stop being a follower&nbsp;
and start becoming a leader. To most of us,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:58.480
this probably seems like a fair thing to say.&nbsp;
But, to the CCP, this comes of a criticism.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:03.840
To them, Jack is essentially saying that the&nbsp;
CCP is making China into a follower instead of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:08.880
a leader. Moving onto Jack’s second point, he went&nbsp;
onto discuss how we need to take responsibility&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:14.000
for the future. This part of the speech&nbsp;
would’ve probably been if it wasn’t for this one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:19.920
quote from President Xi Jinping. Apparently,&nbsp;
the president told Jack “success does not have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:25.840
to be with me.” I think it’s quite possible that&nbsp;
President Jinping really did mean what he said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:31.200
but I don’t think he completed his full thought.&nbsp;
I think the full thought goes something like this:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:38.080
“success does not have to be with me, but&nbsp;
control does”. By sharing just the first part,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:44.320
I think Jack gave his peers and everyday Chinese a&nbsp;
sense a freedom that the CCP was not a fan of. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:50.000
this statement didn’t push the CCP over the edge,&nbsp;
the next part of Jack’s speech definitely did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:54.400
as Jack would go onto to outrightly&nbsp;
criticize the Chinese financial system.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:59.760
He said that “Today’s financial system is a&nbsp;
product of the industrial age.” In other words,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:05.360
he was suggesting that China’s financial system&nbsp;
was centuries behind. The nail in the coffin was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:10.240
“We cannot regulate the future with yesterday’s&nbsp;
means. There’s no systemic financial risks in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:16.080
China because there’s no financial system&nbsp;
in China. The risks are a lack of systems.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:23.040
By this point, Jack was already done for and it&nbsp;
was probably best if stopped talking, but he would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:29.440
go onto talk about the CCP’s least favorite word:&nbsp;
Reform. “The new financial system is the direction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:35.600
of the future. No matter whether we are happy or&nbsp;
not, it will definitely rise. No matter whether we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:42.400
do it or not, someone will do it. In the future,&nbsp;
I believe that reform is a sacrifice and a price.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:48.800
After that statement, Jack almost sounds like&nbsp;
a revolutionary. For obvious reasons, the CCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:54.880
is no fan of revolutionaries and they would make&nbsp;
that crystal clear in the coming weeks and months.

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:59.200
THE AFTERMATH:&nbsp;

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:04.080
Shortly after Jack’s hero moment, he would be&nbsp;
invited to a closed-door meeting with Chinese&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:10.080
financial regulators. As you would guess, this&nbsp;
meeting wasn’t to go through his proposed changes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:15.653
It was actually to inform him that the Ant Group&nbsp;
IPO would not be allowed to take place. In a last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.653 --> 00:06:19.920
ditch effort, Jack would try to bribe them with a&nbsp;
stake in the Ant Group. Jack told them, “You can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:26.320
take any of the platforms Ant has, as long as the&nbsp;
country needs it.” But, the CCP was by no means&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:31.760
willing to let Jack go so easily. It was clear to&nbsp;
them that they had to make an example out of Jack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:36.800
to prevent other billionaries from stepping out&nbsp;
of line. And that’s exactly what they would do.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:43.120
After cancelling the Ant Group IPO, they would&nbsp;
cancel all of his public appearances. They even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:48.640
replaced him as a judge on his own talent show&nbsp;
called “Africa’s Business Heroes”. That would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:54.160
like America’s Got Talent replacing Simon Cowell&nbsp;
without his consent. Over the next few months,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:59.440
Jack would completely disappear from the spotlight&nbsp;
and this is why we got all those articles asking:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:05.040
Where’s Jack. The official explanation is that&nbsp;
Jack was simply laying low while things were hot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:11.440
but it’s very possible that Jack was detained&nbsp;
or even tortured. Even if Jack wasn’t beaten,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:16.640
there’s no questions that his companies&nbsp;
were being beaten. On December 23, 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:22.320
China would launch an antitrust investigation&nbsp;
into Alibaba for suspected monopolistic practices.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:26.560
Around the same time, they would tell the Ant&nbsp;
Group that they need to substantially reduce their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:31.280
scope. They were instructed to stop pursuing&nbsp;
the insurance and wealth management sectors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:36.200
and simply stick to payment services. China&nbsp;
would also move to make the Ant Group a state&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:41.520
owned operation. China would force existing&nbsp;
shareholders to give up half of their equity to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:46.640
6 outside shareholders. This included&nbsp;
a 15% stake to Nanyang Commercial Bank,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:52.320
5% to China Huarong Asset Management, and 10%&nbsp;
to Cathay United Bank. A few months later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:59.120
China would hit Alibaba with a record $2.8 billion&nbsp;
fine. They would also delete Alibaba’s internet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:04.720
browser from the app store. Alibaba’s browser&nbsp;
was the second most popular web browser in China&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:10.080
before it was deleted. While such moves were&nbsp;
no doubt painful, most of the damage actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:15.200
came from how people perceived these moves.&nbsp;
You see, customers nor investors want to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:19.920
associated with Chinese companies that aren’t&nbsp;
friends with the CCP for obvious reasons. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:26.320
they both started leaving in droves. I mean just&nbsp;
look at what happened to Alibaba stock. The worst&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:32.000
part was that Jack’s actions didn’t just hurt&nbsp;
his own companies but all Chinese companies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:36.720
Jack’s speech made it clear to the CCP that&nbsp;
they had not only given Jack too much freedom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:42.640
but all billionaires too much freedom. So, they&nbsp;
thought it was best to punish them all. And if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:48.720
don’t believe me, just take a look at the Nasdaq&nbsp;
Golden Dragon China Index. This is an index of 30&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:56.400
of the strongest companies in China. And this&nbsp;
index wasn’t down 20, 30, 40, or even 50%. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.400 --> 00:09:07.840
was down 76% and we still don’t know if the bottom&nbsp;
is in. Clearly, Jack has created quite a disaster.

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:11.040
DESTROYING HIS LEGACY:
Once the initial damage had been dealt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:16.880
to Jack’s companies, the CCP switched their focus&nbsp;
to destroying his legacy. And the way they’ve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:22.480
been accomplishing this is by stripping him of&nbsp;
all of his positive associations. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:27.840
one of Jack’s contributions was creating a&nbsp;
university called Hupan University in 2015.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:31.920
The university was a business school&nbsp;
focused on creating the next generation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:37.120
of business leaders. Jack felt that this was&nbsp;
China’s version of Harvard Business School&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:41.040
and there was no doubt that it&nbsp;
was an extremely elite school.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:46.480
After all, you needed to own a business that was&nbsp;
pulling in at least $4.5 million in revenue per&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:53.040
year to even apply to the school. This school is&nbsp;
no doubt one of Jack’s proudest contributions, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:58.480
the CCP has been actively trying to dismantle the&nbsp;
entire thing. First of all, they forced the school&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:04.880
to suspend enrollments. Then, they removed Jack as&nbsp;
president of the school. And finally, they forced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:10.160
the institutions to drop the word “University”&nbsp;
from its name. The new name of the institution&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:15.680
is the Hupan Innovation Center. All of these moves&nbsp;
are clearly geared to discredit the institution as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:20.720
much as possible. Also, Jack Ma was one of the&nbsp;
main factors attracting students to the school,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:25.440
and if he’s no longer associated with the&nbsp;
school, why would anybody bother joining?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:31.600
Jack’s goal was for Hupan to run for 300 years,&nbsp;
but at this point, it’s not clear if Hupan will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:36.800
last even 30 years. In the meantime, Alibaba has&nbsp;
resorted to trying to bribe themselves back into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:42.960
the CCP’s good graces. Late last year for example,&nbsp;
Alibaba announced that they would make a $15.5&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:48.160
billion donation to China’s common prosperity&nbsp;
fund. For perspective, this figure was equivalent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:53.920
to ⅓ of their entire cash reserves. This just&nbsp;
shows how desperate Alibaba is to get back on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.920 --> 00:11:00.000
the CCP’s good side. The CCP of course accepted&nbsp;
the donation, but it doesn’t look like Alibaba&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:05.280
is in the green just yet. More likely than not,&nbsp;
this is gonna be a several year journey for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:13.840
Alibaba to slowly earn back their freedoms&nbsp;
and Jack will have nothing to do with it.

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:16.480
JACK MA TODAY:
Today, it seems like Jack has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:24.160
more or less accepted. He rolled the dice with the&nbsp;
CCP and the CCP has shown him who’s truly on top.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:30.560
At this point, he’s still got plenty of money,&nbsp;
but he’s lost everything that gave him purpose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:37.280
whether that be his talent show or his university&nbsp;
or even just control over his own companies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:43.200
The CCP basically told him, you went too far.&nbsp;
We’ll let you keep your money, but you’re gonna&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:49.200
have to give up everything else. For a lot of&nbsp;
you, this probably doesn’t seem that bad. I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:54.960
in the end, he does still have $30 billion,&nbsp;
so things could definitely be a lot worse.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.600 --> 00:11:59.600
Looking forward, if Jack simply sticks&nbsp;
to enjoying his wealth inside China,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:04.880
he probably won’t have any further issues. If he&nbsp;
tries to invest his money into a new business or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:11.120
new endeavor, however, the CCP probably won’t&nbsp;
be very happy. And they’ll likely start this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:17.280
whole takedown process all over again, and this&nbsp;
time they won’t leave him with any money either.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:22.160
So, for his own good, it’s best if Jack&nbsp;
sticks to private jets and mansions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:27.440
instead of change and revolution, but that’s&nbsp;
just what I think. If you were Jack, would you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:33.920
have criticized the CCP? Comment that down below.&nbsp;
Also, drop a like if you’re not a fan of the CCP.&nbsp;&nbsp;

